 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Glared gleam from the lurid sky\nOn flood of feverly eye\nOf languor on the dying,\nBlack as hell in blackest night. Title.\nThe writhing winds were dead again,\nThe windless skies they seem'd not remain;\nAnd as, where once the heavy sunlight\nBrewled darkness, now the twilight\nPeered all the woods with shadows,\nSo, when the stars stood still alone,\nAll things seemed an agony a-wailin' and\nA sound of anguish for half a second",
